## Verification — the definition of done

{{VERIFICATION_SECTION}}

Never declare a change "done" on reasoning alone — the checks above must be green. AI review judges architecture and requirement coverage; deterministic tools judge correctness.

## Boundaries

- Stay in task scope; no drive-by refactors or unrelated "cleanups".
- No new dependencies without justification and approval.
- Never commit or push without explicit approval; draft the message, the human decides.
- Never modify CI, deployment config, secrets, or environment files without explicit approval.
- Match the style of the file being edited; preserve working behavior.
{{EXTRA_BOUNDARIES}}

